// ─── Where money sits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// An account is a position with an institution:
// - a deposit that Chase owes Sam;
// - a card on which Sam owes Chase;
// - shares that Fidelity keeps for him.
//
// The institution holds the money and Sam owns it: custody and ownership
// are separate facts.
//
// Money that sits in no account is with its owner. That covers cash in hand,
// the condo and the laptop. There are no income, expense or equity accounts:
// what a flow was for is its purpose, and whom it was with is its party.

account checking   : deposit at chase
account savings    : deposit at chase
account visa       : card at chase
account fidelity-brokerage : brokerage
account retirement : 401k at fidelity
  employer lumen
account escrow     : escrow at rocket   // property tax and insurance, held by the lender
